The parallelogram formed by folding the triangle over its angle bisectors is also called the Varignon parallelogram.  A vertex of it is the midpoint of the third side of the triangle, while the other three vertices are the feet of the three angle-bisector altitudes forming a smaller triangle.  The sides of the smaller triangle are parallel to the corresponding sides of the median triangle, so the area of the smaller triangle is proportional to the area of the median triangle by the square of the ratio of the medians.  The ratio of the medians is proportional to the ratio of the centers of gravity of the triangles, which also means area ratios.  The centroid of the $triangle ABD$ divides the median in a ratio of 2 to 1 (plus the fact that $BDC$ is also a triangle), so the length of $BF$ is $2(\frac{2}{3}AB)=2\times\frac{20}{3}=\frac{40}{3}$. The smaller triangle $BFD$ has one semiperimeter of $\frac{BF+DF+BD}{2}=\frac{\frac{40}{3}+\frac{20}{3}+ \frac{21}{3}}{2}=\frac{81}{6}$ and area:
$$\begin{aligned} 
S_{BFD}&=\sqrt{ \frac{81}{6}\left(\frac{81}{6}- \frac{40}{3}\right)\left(\frac{81}{6}- \frac{20}{3}\right)\left(\frac{81}{6}- \frac{21}{3}\right)}\qquad & \\ 
&= \frac{3}{2}\sqrt{5933} \approx 51.1\qquad & \end{aligned}$$
The area of the original triangle thus is $511$, and the square root of $5933$ is between $77$ and $78$, so the ratio of the areas is between $49$ and $56$.  Then $r$, as proportion of the median, is between $\frac{49}{5933}\times \frac{40}{3}$ and $\frac{56}{5933}\times \frac{40}{3}$, which are approximately $0.0051$ and $0.0143$.  In $r$, these values round to $5.1\times10^{-3}$ and $1.4\times10^{-2}$, respectively.
