\[f(a, c) = \sqrt{c(a - c)} + \sqrt{c(16 - a - c)}.\]Since $f(a + b, c)$ isipedal on $a,$ there exists a value $c_0 \le \frac{a + b}{2} = 8$ such that
\[\sqrt{c_0(a - c_0)} = \sqrt{c_0(b - c_0)}.\]Squaring both sides, we get
\[c_0(a + b - 2c_0) = a - b.\]Substituting $b = 16 - a,$ we get
\[c_0(16 - 2c_0) = 2a - 16,\]so
\[c_0 = \sqrt{a + a - 8} = \sqrt{2a - 8}.\]The expression to maximize is
\[\sqrt{c(a - c)} + \sqrt{c(8 - c)},\]and
\[\sqrt{c(8 - c)} = \sqrt{c(8 - \sqrt{2a - 8})}.\]Since $4c - c(a - c) \le 4,$ $c \le \frac{4}{a + 1},$ so
