We have $$\cos(\sin(x))=\cos(-\sin(x))=\cos(\sin(x)).$$A full increase in $\sin(x)$ is another full decrease, i.e. $2\pi$ units, but we're not trying to maximize $\sin(x)$, we're trying to find the period of the function $\cos(\sin(x))$, so we see that $2\pi$ already works (we'll see that there is no smaller $T>0$ such that $\cos(\sin(x+T))=\cos(\sin(x))$ for all $x$). Hence the answer is $\boxed{2\pi}$.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

real func (real x) {
  return(cos(sin(x)));
}

draw(graph(func,-12*pi,12*pi),red);
draw((-12*pi,0)--(-12*pi,2.5),dashed);
draw((12*pi,0)--(12*pi,2.5),dashed);
