We have
\begin{align*}
\sin 2t &= 2 \sin t \cos t, \\
\sin^2 t &= \frac{1 - \cos 2t}{2}, \\
\cos^2 t &= 1 - \sin^2 t = \frac{1 + \cos 2t}{2}.
\end{align*}Then
\begin{align*}
2x^2 y &= 2 \sin^2 t \sin 2t \\
&= 2 \sin^2 t (2 \sin t \cos t) \\
&= \left( \frac{4 \sin^5 t}{\cos t} \right) + \left( \frac{8 \sin^3 t \cos t}{\cos t} \right)
\end{align*}By the AM-GM Inequality,
\[2 \sqrt{\frac{4 \sin^5 t}{\cos t} \cdot \left( \frac{8 \sin^3 t}{\cos t} \right)} \ge 2x^2 y,\]or
\[\frac{32 \sin^8 t}{\cos^2 t} \ge 4 x^2 y.\]Therefore,
\[\frac{1}{16} \cdot \frac{32 \sin^8 t}{\cos^2 t} \ge \frac{1}{16} \cdot 4 x^2 y,\]or
\[\cos^2 t \ge 2 \cos^2 t - x^2 y.\]Then
\[\sin^2 t \cos^2 t \ge 2 \sin^2 t \cos^2 t - x^2 y \sin^2 t,\]or
\[2 \sin^2 t \cos^2 t + x^2 y \sin^2 t \le \sin^2 t,\]or
\[\sin^4 t + x^2 y \sin^2 t \le \frac{1}{2}.\]Then
\[\cos^2 t \sin^4 t + x^2 y \cos^2 t \sin^2 t \le \frac{1}{2} \cos^2 t,\]or
\[x^4 - 2 x^2 + 1 + x^2 y = \cos^2 t \sin^2 t (\cos^2 t - 2) + 1 \le \frac{1}{2} \cos^2 t.\]It follows that $a = 1,$ $b = 2,$ $c = \frac{1}{2},$ so $a + b + c = 1 + 2 + \frac{1}{2} = \boxed{\frac{7}{2}}.$

