For all $x \in [-1, 1],$ $\arcsin x + \arccos x = \frac{\pi}{2}.$  Squaring both sides, we get
\begin{align*}
(\arcsin x + \arccos x)^2 &= \left( \frac{\pi}{2} \right)^2, \\
(\arcsin x)^2 + (\arccos x)^2 + 2 (\arcsin x) (\arccos x) &= \frac{\pi^2}{4},
\end{align*}so
\[f(x) + 2(\arcsin x) (\arccos x) = \frac{\pi^2}{4}.\]Thus,
\[f(x) = \frac{\pi^2}{4} - 2 (\arcsin x) (\arccos x).\]Because $-\frac{\pi}{2} \leq \arcsin x \leq \frac{\pi}{2},$ we have
\[-\frac{\pi}{2} \leq \arcsin x \leq \arccos x \leq \frac{\pi}{2}.\]Hence,
\[- \frac{\pi^2}{4} \leq (\arccos x) (\arcsin x) \leq \frac{\pi^2}{16}.\]Then
\[- \frac{\pi^2}{16} \leq - 2 (\arcsin x) (\arccos x) \leq \frac{\pi^2}{4}.\]Therefore,
\[\frac{\pi^2}{4} - \frac{\pi^2}{16} \leq \frac{\pi^2}{4} - 2 (\arcsin x) (\arccos x) \leq \frac{\pi^2}{4} + \frac{\pi^2}{4},\]and
